{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You are children to YHWH your Elohim.</b> This section is joined to the section of the seduced city to teach that it is forbidden to mourn over the dead of the seduced city — a man for his son or for his brother; and He forbade gashing the flesh for the dead, which is what is meant by 'you shall not gash yourselves.' Now the custom of the Amorites was so because they made this world the essence, and when one of them died and was lost from among them, behold he is lost forever; but you are not so, for 'you are children to YHWH your Elohim,' and it is the way of a father to bequeath to his son the finest portion that he has; therefore the World to Come that I have created is prepared for you, and accordingly you are not permitted to gash yourselves over the dead nor to pluck out the hair of the head, for you are confident that even if the body perishes in this world, you will inherit the life of the World to Come, which is the essence. And this is what is said: 'for you are a holy people to YHWH your Elohim.' And the meaning of 'holy' is set apart — He says: because you are set apart from the rest of the children of Noah, in the manner of what is said (Leviticus 20:26): ״ואבדיל אתכם מן העמים להיות לי״. And His saying 'for you are a holy people to YHWH your Elohim' further includes the concept of the reward of the World to Come — He says: because you are a people cleaving to the holy El, and you are prepared for this exalted rank, which is the rank of the World to Come, it is not fitting for you to do what they do."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:15.777026756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}